# tier-budget-allowlist — today's per-tier budget violators (law-unit-tests-run-under-a-second;
# test plan §4.1), and the wall time each was measured at when seeded.
#
# spira/tier-budget.sh checks every suite's tier (# tier: header; untagged counts as T1)
# against its budget: T0/T1 1000ms, T2 10s, T3 60s. A suite NOT on this list is held to that
# budget outright. A suite ON this list fails only if it gets slower than its recorded time
# here, plus SPIRA_TIER_ALLOWLIST_MARGIN_PCT (default 20%) for load noise — the ratchet that
# lets the hard rule land without every suite in the corpus going red on the same day.
#
# THE ALLOWLIST CAN ONLY SHRINK. spira/tier-budget.sh lint-allowlist fails a branch that adds
# an entry or raises a recorded time; it does not fail one that removes an entry or lowers a
# time. Rewrite a suite to fit its tier's budget (or lower) and delete its line here — that is
# the only way this file is meant to change size.
#
# FORMAT: one entry per line, tab-separated: <suite> <tier> <seconds>. <tier> is the entry's
# tier at seed time, used only so a later re-tiering of the suite does not silently change
# its budget out from under it. Blank lines and `#` comments are ignored.
